{"archetypes":[{"name":"thin-fence","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Step 3.6 now depends on a new shell driver/orchestrator boundary with FD and rc semantics that can regress quietly.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the thin orchestrator fence captures driver output, preserves quiet-mode FD semantics, and branches only on the documented return codes. Check that displayed output and parser-only control data remain separated across the SKILL.md fence and the driver. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"trailer-parser","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The rc=10 Continue/Stop path relies on exact trusted-trailer parsing and spoof resistance.","prompt_body":"Review the rc=10 trusted trailer implementation end to end, especially last-marker selection, numeric round validation, display filtering, and fail-closed behavior on missing or malformed trailers. Look for paths where spoofed assessor prose, stale env files, or fallback parsing could influence the Stop round. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"classification-gate","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Classification resolution now controls SIMPLE skips, HARD assessment, snapshots, and child assessment behavior.","prompt_body":"Check every new design_classification gate and override path for consistent fail-closed HARD behavior. Compare the orchestrator, postplan snapshot gating, and assess-plan-round child override to ensure legacy workflow_path cannot incorrectly suppress HARD behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pause-resume","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Pause handling moved between driver and orchestrator while Step 3.6 was inserted into resume ordering.","prompt_body":"Examine pause-before-gate, rc=11 handoff, and completion-sentinel behavior around Step 3, Step 3.5, Step 3.6, and Step 3b. Verify skipped Gate-B paths and resumed sessions cannot re-enter intentionally skipped review or assessor work. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sidecar-taint","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Verdict sidecars and model-derived fields are now rendered through shell parsing and display neutralization paths.","prompt_body":"Inspect handling of assessor verdict env sidecars and QUALIFICATIONS_SUMMARY as untrusted data. Look for sourcing, evaluation, shell expansion, insufficient literal key parsing, or incomplete neutralization of marker-like display lines before emit. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
